@extends('layouts/marketing')

<script server>
useSeoMeta({
  title: 'loghq vs Rollbar - loghq',
  description: 'How loghq, an open-source error tracker you self-host on Postgres, compares to Rollbar’s closed-source SaaS.',
  ogImage: 'https://loghq.org/og.png',
})
useHead({ link: [{ rel: 'canonical', href: 'https://loghq.org/compare/rollbar' }] })

// Breadcrumb trail. One array drives two consumers — the rendered list in
// the Breadcrumbs partial and the BreadcrumbList JSON-LD below — so the
// markup and the structured data cannot disagree. The last crumb has no
// href or url: it is this page.
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/', url: 'https://loghq.org/' },
  { label: 'Compare', href: '/compare', url: 'https://loghq.org/compare' },
  { label: 'Rollbar' },
]
</script>

@push('styles')
<style>
  /* Highlight the loghq column (2nd of every 3 grid cells) so the table reads
    at a glance. Uses the same accent-soft token as the rest of the site. */
  .cmp-hl .cmp-cell:nth-child(3n+2) { background: var(--accent-soft); }
  .cmp-note { margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--text-3); font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 68ch; }
</style>
@endpush

@section('content')
@structuredData({
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: crumbs.map((c, i) => ({ '@type': 'ListItem', position: i + 1, name: c.label, item: c.url })),
})

@include('Breadcrumbs')

<section class="feat-hero shell">
  <span class="kicker">Compare</span>
  <h1>loghq vs Rollbar</h1>
  <p>Rollbar is a mature, closed-source SaaS error tracker with fine-grained grouping controls and a query language for shaping how issues fold together. loghq covers the same core loop, capture, group, source-map, and alert, as open source you can self-host, so sensitive stack data never leaves your own servers.</p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <StxLink class="btn primary" to="/register">Get started</StxLink>
    <StxLink class="btn ghost" to="/compare">All alternatives</StxLink>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reveal section shell" aria-labelledby="table-heading">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 id="table-heading" class="section-title">loghq and Rollbar, side by side</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="cmp cmp-hl">
  <div class="cmp-cell">Capability</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">loghq</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Rollbar</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">What it is</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost">Focused error and crash tracking</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Error tracking</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Open source</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost">Yes, open source</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">No</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Self-host / data ownership</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost">Yes, your own Postgres</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">No, SaaS only</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Pricing model</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost">Free self-hosted, usage-based hosted</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Event-volume based</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Error grouping</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost">Automatic fingerprinting</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Yes, rule-based grouping</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Source maps and stack traces</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost">Full source-mapped traces</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Yes</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Releases and environments</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost">Built in</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Yes</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Alerting</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost">New and spiking issues</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Yes</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Data retention</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost">Yours to set when self-hosted</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Plan-based</div>
  </div>
  <p class="cmp-note">Where Rollbar still leads: its rule-based grouping and item-query language give power users a lot of manual control over how errors are bucketed.</p>
</section>

<section class="reveal section shell" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 id="why-heading" class="section-title">Why teams pick loghq</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="flow">
    <div class="flow-step">
      <span class="flow-num">01</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Own your data</h3>
        <p>Rollbar is SaaS only. loghq self-hosts on your own Postgres, keeping error data inside your infrastructure by default.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-step">
      <span class="flow-num">02</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Open source</h3>
        <p>loghq is open, so grouping behavior and ingestion are transparent and yours to tune in code, not a black box.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-step">
      <span class="flow-num">03</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Predictable cost</h3>
        <p>Event-volume pricing spikes exactly when you have an incident and traffic. Self-hosted loghq removes that link entirely.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reveal section shell" aria-label="Fair comparison">
  <div class="chips">
    <div class="chip">
      <h3>Credit where it is due</h3>
      <p>Rollbar’s grouping controls are more configurable out of the box than most trackers. loghq leans on automatic fingerprinting that is right most of the time and simpler to live with.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="chip">
      <h3>What loghq is</h3>
      <p>Open-source error and crash tracking you can run on your own Postgres, or use on a hosted tier. Automatic capture, fingerprint grouping, source-mapped traces, releases, and alerts, without the rest of an observability suite.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reveal section shell" aria-labelledby="related-heading">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 id="related-heading" class="section-title">More comparisons</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="related">
    <StxLink to="/compare/sentry">
      <div class="r-name">loghq vs Sentry</div>
      <div class="r-desc">The incumbent error platform, compared.</div>
    </StxLink>
    <StxLink to="/compare/airbrake">
      <div class="r-name">loghq vs Airbrake</div>
      <div class="r-desc">One of the original error trackers.</div>
    </StxLink>
    <StxLink to="/compare/honeybadger">
      <div class="r-name">loghq vs Honeybadger</div>
      <div class="r-desc">Errors plus uptime and cron monitoring.</div>
    </StxLink>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reveal section shell" aria-label="Get started">
  <div class="cta-band">
    <h2>Own your error tracking.</h2>
    <div class="cta-actions">
      <StxLink class="btn primary" to="/register">Get started</StxLink>
      <StxLink class="btn ghost" to="/features/self-host">Read about self-hosting</StxLink>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
@endsection
